{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789544895,"nonce":"V5XfYCZ6uLZPzYHpMipgyqi3mGY=","title":"frozenset for nqueens and meteor-contest","message":"The unedited nqueens kernel stops at line 39 on `frozenset(row[0])` with `calling name is not supported yet`. After bisect landed in 6f4943746ea3eedfad41da7ff353184c3cd0d545, meteor-contest gets past its import and stops at line 57 on `frozenset([cti[c + o] for o in pp if (c + o) in cti])` with the same error.\n\nThese kernels also pass `frozenset` as a value to `map`, compare frozensets inside sets, use set subtraction and membership, and nqueens calls `frozenset.union(ar, ac, ad, ag)`. The result needs immutable set identity and equality independent of insertion order. In particular, treating it as an ordinary mutable set would let `.add` mutate it and produce the wrong type/repr. Check each kernel answer against CPython before a speed verdict. Related: nqueens issue 941c59b, bisect issue 361cabd, kernel index 89aaf85.","files":null}]}